From 63d927a5226baf0d40d62cb4aa9fb94ab1337b0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:42:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] media: v4l2-jpeg: bound jpeg_skip() by the bytes left
To: Mauro Carvalho Chehab <mchehab@kernel.org>
Cc: Hans Verkuil <hverkuil@kernel.org>,
    Philipp Zabel <p.zabel@pengutronix.de>,
    Mirela Rabulea <mirela.rabulea@nxp.com>,
    imx@lists.linux.dev,
    linux-media@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

The segment parsers compute lengths as int and pass them to
jpeg_skip(), which takes a size_t. A negative length becomes a huge
one, stream->curr + len wraps to a position before the current one,
and the bounds check passes, so parsing moves backwards instead of
failing.

After the DHT and DQT fixes earlier in this series only the APP14
parser still does that: an APP14 segment shorter than its length field
says, or an "Adobe" one shorter than 14 bytes, is accepted, an Adobe
one with a transform flag read from the next segment.

Compare the length with the bytes left instead of computing a pointer
past the buffer, so a negative length fails.

This depends on commit "media: v4l2-jpeg: fix the end of DHT segment
parsing": without it every DHT segment would fail here.

Fixes: 50733b5b9102 ("media: add v4l2 JPEG helpers")
Fixes: b8035f7988a8 ("media: Add parsing for APP14 data segment in jpeg helpers")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c
index c2b4761b3..0258abdfb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c
@@ -203,7 +203,12 @@ static int jpeg_get_word_be(struct jpeg_stream *stream)
 
 static int jpeg_skip(struct jpeg_stream *stream, size_t len)
 {
-	if (stream->curr + len > stream->end)
+	/*
+	 * Callers compute lengths as int: a negative one becomes a huge size_t
+	 * here. Compare with the bytes left, so the pointer addition can
+	 * neither wrap nor move backwards.
+	 */
+	if (len > (size_t)(stream->end - stream->curr))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	stream->curr += len;
-- 
